<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Newton returns for his preventive visit at 50, two weeks after starting sertraline 50 mg and three and a half weeks after the laboratory was closed. His cold cleared within five days without antibiotics. He completed the health risk questionnaire beforehand. He has no side effects from sertraline now, has missed no doses, and has had two sessions of cognitive behavioral therapy. He sleeps about five hours, keeps a fixed rising time, and no longer dozes in his chair in the evening. He eats three small meals a day and has gained 0.5 kg. His mood is a little better; he has written to the friends he accused to apologize. He has had no thoughts of death or of harming himself or anyone else. He has never had colorectal cancer screening. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Preventive health visit, age 50</td></tr><tr><td>Active conditions</td><td>Major depression on sertraline and CBT; insomnia improving with CBT-I; raised urine mercury after removal from exposure</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Sertraline 50 mg; acetaminophen no longer needed</td></tr><tr><td>Screening history</td><td>No colorectal screening; HIV and hepatitis C tests negative in his forties</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient before the visit and reviewed during the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Fair, improving</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Lives alone; repairing strained friendships; no financial worries</td></tr><tr><td>Behavioral</td><td>Never smoker; wine rarely (AUDIT-C 1); walks about 30 minutes most days; diet plain and irregular until recently</td></tr><tr><td>Occupational</td><td>Laboratory closed pending decontamination and a fume hood; teaching continues</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent</td></tr><tr><td>Home safety</td><td>Smoke and carbon monoxide detectors in his rooms; no firearms</td></tr><tr><td>Sexual health</td><td>Not sexually active; no risk factors for sexually transmitted infection</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>Hears well; reading glasses; eye examination two years ago</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>About five hours a night, improving with CBT-I</td></tr><tr><td>Pain</td><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

