    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Preventive health visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and a personalized prevention plan made. His main risks are the depressive episode and the recent occupational exposure, both under treatment; lipids are normal. [S]<list><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Major depressive disorder (F32.2)</content>. PHQ-9 16, down from 20, two weeks into sertraline 50 mg; no side effects now and no missed doses; no suicidal thoughts or thoughts of harming others. [S]<list><item>Continue sertraline 50 mg and weekly CBT; depression review in one week as planned.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Acute viral upper respiratory infection (J06.9)</content>. Resolved within five days. [S]<list><item>No further action.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Influenza vaccine, this season</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Given today</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal conjugate vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PCV20 given today; recommended for all adults aged 50 and over</td></tr><tr><td>Recombinant zoster vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Dose 1 given today; dose 2 due in two to six months</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine, this season</td><td>Due</td><td>He preferred not to have a fourth injection today and will have it at his pharmacy within the month</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus booster</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap six years ago</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Two-dose adult series completed seven years ago</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Never screened; he chose a yearly fecal immunochemical test over colonoscopy; kit given today</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 16 while under treatment</td></tr><tr><td>Lipid screening and cardiovascular risk</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Total cholesterol 176 mg/dL, HDL 61 mg/dL, LDL 98 mg/dL, triglycerides 86 mg/dL; blood pressure 120/76 mmHg; never smoker; low 10-year risk, so no statin</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>BMI 22.2 and no other risk factors; glucose 88 mg/dL at intake</td></tr><tr><td>HIV and hepatitis C screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>One-time tests negative in his forties</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol misuse screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C 1</td></tr><tr><td>Prostate cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Shared decision about PSA screening is offered from 55; he has no family history known to him</td></tr><tr><td>Lung cancer and abdominal aortic aneurysm screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Never smoker</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>Up to date</td><td>No concerns; eye examination two years ago</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Influenza vaccine, 1693-1694 season; Pneumococcal conjugate vaccine PCV20; Recombinant zoster vaccine, dose 1 of 2 [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monograph (2026); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026); Expanded Recommendations for Use of Pneumococcal Conjugate Vaccines Among Adults Aged ≥50 Years: Recommendations of the Advisory Committee on Immunization Practices (2024); Colorectal Cancer: Screening (2021); Depression and Suicide Risk in Adults: Screening (2023); Statin Use for the Primary Prevention of Cardiovascular Disease in Adults: Preventive Medication (2022)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Depression and exposure review in one week as planned, with a repeat 24-hour urine mercury. Second zoster dose in two to six months. Fecal immunochemical test kit to be returned within two weeks. Next scheduled visit 1693-10-29: three-week depression and exposure follow-up with a repeat 24-hour urine mercury. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
